# Situation

Repo: claude-engineering-skills (public), where several AI sessions open pull requests in parallel, each branch squash-merged to `main`. A required `full-suite` GitHub Actions check gives the verdict on a PR; a PR that GitHub marks CONFLICTING gets no `pull_request` workflow run at all, so it gets no verdict and cannot be merged until someone rebases it by hand.

The maintainer replayed every merge of `main` into the PR branches of #236-#253 with `git merge-tree` (measured 2026-10-15) and reports: 13 of the 16 conflicted. `skills.manifest.json` conflicted 9 times, every time on the single `bundleVersion` line; `docs/plans/README.md` 8 times, every time on its summary-counts line; `status.md` twice. `bundleVersion` is a hash over every skill file, so any PR that edits any skill file moves it, and two such PRs always collide.

The repo's policy for generated files (below) currently files `skills.manifest.json` under Category B: committed and freshness-verified by `skills:check` in the pre-push `check`. It is a pure, deterministic function of `skills/**`; regenerating it twice on one commit is byte-identical, which is what put it in B. This question concerns that one file. (The plans-index counts are a separate decision.)

